    "tree_id": "d6a6a5588c1687645fb5850f868a770941609d77",
    "message": "Share one service module at the entry point, and keep a stopped post's draft.\n\npython -m loads this file as __main__, so the poster was reading a second before_send. The entry point now calls the package module's main. A stop during the post listing goes through pause_post instead of being stored as superseded.\n\ntest_the_module_entry_shares_the_poster_hook fails when the guard calls this file's own main. test_a_stop_during_the_post_keeps_the_draft fails when that stop is settled as superseded.\n\nCo-authored-by: Brandon Dees <brandondees@users.noreply.github.com>",
